**How to implement.** Every Materials window carries the app's import seam, the one a Sample editor opens in Select state included, so a file dropped on it is decided against the app library (001 §H: dropped onto the Library or Materials window; the S3.2 brief). This step threads the seam and changes no behaviour; step 110 reads it. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`) gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories`, documented as the import seam that dropped entry files are decided and applied through. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`: `MaterialsWindow` (`MaterialsWindow.fs:29`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories` and sets the context field. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SampleEditorWindow.fs`: `SampleEditorWindow` (`SampleEditorWindow.fs:30`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories` and passes it to the Select-state `MaterialsWindow` that its `openMaterialsSelect` builds (`SampleEditorWindow.fs:69`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs`: the Sample editor it opens (`LibraryWindow.fs:77`) gets the window's `catalogueImports` (step 101). (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `EditorLaunchers.openMaterialsWindow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:150`) takes the `CatalogueImportContext` after the `CategoryProxy`; `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it to `MaterialsWindow` (`:193`); and the strip's `OpenMaterialsWindow` (`:1832`) passes `model.catalogueImports` (step 101). The field's doc names the import seam in no more words. (6) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: the launcher's Materials button passes `context.catalogueImports`. (7) Every test construction passes one. `MaterialsWindowTests`' `stubContext` (`MaterialsWindowTests.fs:180`) and its `MaterialsWindow(...)` mounts (`:702`, `:1044`), `SampleEditorWindowTests`' `SampleEditorWindow(...)` mounts, `EmbeddedChartTests`' `MaterialsWindow(...)` (`EmbeddedChartTests.fs:230`), `ScrollExtentTests`' `MaterialsWindow(...)` and `SampleEditorWindow(...)`, `WindowLauncherTests`' windows (`WindowLauncherTests.fs:453`, `:488`, `:545`) and `WireUi0040CompositionTests`' Sample editors (`WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:306`, `:352`) pass `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:47`, `:57`, `:149`) passes `ctx.catalogueImports`, and `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording `openMaterialsWindow` (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:106`) takes the extra argument. `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' launchers, a record update of `EditorLaunchers.defaults` (`WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs:136`), keep their code. A doc that lists the window's stores names the import seam in no more words. No assertion changes: the facts whose constructions change keep what they assert, among them `Library and Materials windows: the facet rows wrap, nothing is clipped`, `Material, Sample, Category and Source editors leave everything reachable`, `the Materials and Library strip buttons reach their launchers as pure launches`, `the initial projection lists every stored material as a selectable entry leaf with the live count`.

**Acceptance.** After the threading, every `MaterialsWindow` and `SampleEditorWindow` construction MUST pass a `CatalogueImportContext`, and no assertion MUST change; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.
